# Pros and cons

### SQS
- Pro: fully managed, nothing to operate.
- Pro: scales automatically past our peak.
- Con: no replay.
- Con: 256 KB message limit.

### Kafka (Amazon MSK)
- Pro: replay up to the retention window.
- Pro: supports stream processing.
- Con: needs partition planning.
- Con: we own broker upgrades.

### RabbitMQ (Amazon MQ)
- Pro: flexible routing through exchanges.
- Con: we would own capacity planning.
- Con: throughput ceiling is the lowest of the three.

# Recommendation

! Use **SQS with FIFO queues keyed by order ID**. It meets per-order ordering, handles 1,800 msg/s with no operational work, and is the cheapest option at $310 a month.

We will revisit this if the analytics team needs event replay in 2027.
